{
  "criteria": [
    {
      "id": "C1",
      "level": "Adequate",
      "mark": 6,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "where": "Introduction",
          "quote": "Thus, only one satellite is required. This also just allows for simplicity in communications, reduces cost, and requires less time to build and launch."
        },
        {
          "where": "Introduction",
          "quote": "The proposed satellite would likely be used by governmental and science agencies (e.g. CSIRO, BOM) for research and/or education."
        },
        {
          "where": "Executive Summary",
          "quote": "The satellite, nicknamed ZYZZsat (Z-axis/Y-axis Zeroed Zoning Satellite), is operated and accessed from Australia ground facilities"
        }
      ],
      "reasoning": "The report clearly explains the reef-monitoring mission, its environmental rationale, and why one spacecraft is proposed. It identifies potential government and scientific users, but does not clearly establish who operates the spacecraft or distinguish operators from customers. The rationale is useful but supported by limited, inconsistently presented references."
    },
    {
      "id": "C2",
      "level": "Adequate",
      "mark": 5,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "where": "Launch",
          "quote": "The proposed satellite will thus use the Vega E rocket as a launch vehicle – launched from the Guiana Space Centre Spaceport."
        },
        {
          "where": "Orbit",
          "quote": "Specifically, an altitude of 600km requires a mean inclination of $ 97.7924^{\\circ} $ for the satellite to remain sun-synchronous."
        },
        {
          "where": "Orbit",
          "quote": "Semi-major axis (a)</td><td>6971km"
        },
        {
          "where": "Ground Control & Communications",
          "quote": "Systems Tool Kit 11 (STK) was used to calculate access periods as seen below:"
        },
        {
          "where": "Mission Duration & EOL",
          "quote": "The most promising alternative is a ‘drag sail’ – a drag-enhancing deorbit device that deploys at the EOL."
        },
        {
          "where": "Image 3",
          "quote": ""
        }
      ],
      "reasoning": "The report presents a launch choice, orbit elements, STK screenshots/access results, a ground facility, and mission duration/EOL concepts. However, launch compatibility and timing are speculative, the RAAN rationale is incorrect, and target imaging capability and revisit are not demonstrated. The contact results contain a duplicated access, and EOL disposal is not quantitatively supported. Software files are not evident in the submission."
    },
    {
      "id": "C3",
      "level": "Adequate",
      "mark": 5,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "where": "Conclusion",
          "quote": "A polar sun-synchronous orbit allows for consistent illumination of the oceans while maintaining a constant sun angle."
        },
        {
          "where": "Conclusion",
          "quote": "The Mt Pleasant Radio Observatory is well-located to receive data from this orbit type constantly and for long durations."
        }
      ],
      "reasoning": "The conclusion recaps the selected launch, orbit, and ground facility and relates them to the mission purpose. It gives little synthesis of the design evidence or its limitations, and its claims about illumination and constant ground access are stronger than the analysis supports."
    },
    {
      "id": "C4",
      "level": "Adequate",
      "mark": 4,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "where": "Executive Summary",
          "quote": "This report outlines the intended designs and procedures involved in the construction of a Earth observation satellite"
        },
        {
          "where": "Ground Control & Communications",
          "quote": "DN path for orbits 1-15"
        },
        {
          "where": "Bibliography",
          "quote": "[6] https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2021_in_spaceflight. [Online]."
        }
      ],
      "reasoning": "The report has a clear overall sequence, headings, an executive summary, and supporting images and data. However, writing and formatting are uneven, figures are not fully numbered and titled, and some in-text references do not match the bibliography. Wikipedia is used as a source despite the assignment's restriction."
    }
  ],
